node_modules/
.next/
.env
.env.local
.wrangler/
.dev.vars
/dist/
.vinext/
.coverage/
.ci/
# Transient collect-budget reporter output: the soft-gate sidecar, the run report
# the `collect:stale` gate step and the `collect:gates` summary read, and the
# proposal the `collect:propose` job writes for its artifact/comment.
.freebuff/.collect-budget-soft.json
.freebuff/.collect-budget-run.json
# The verification queue's armed alarm publishes its judgement here — the rows (handles
# and waits, oldest first) the nightly report's alarm section renders, written by the
# armed test, cleared by the runner per attempt, carried in the `--json` report. Transient,
# like the reporter's sidecars above; the file's one spelling and shape are
# `.freebuff/queue-alarm-verdict.mjs`'s.
.freebuff/.ci-queue-alarm-verdict.json
.freebuff/collect-budget-proposal.md
.freebuff/.collect-budget-proposal.json
.freebuff/collect-apply-pr.md
.freebuff/.collect-budget-samples/
.freebuff/collect-gates.md
# The floor proposal the nightly job opens when a reading steps below the floor its records have
# settled to: the writer step derives it from those records (`.freebuff/coverage-trend.mjs
# --propose-low-water`) and the step after it opens the pull request with it as the body. A
# transient of the run, like the collect-budget proposal above it, and regenerable by hand with
# `npm run coverage:propose-low-water`.
.freebuff/coverage-floor-proposal.md
# The coverage readings the suite's guards publish — the rendered-links guard's
# destinations, the frozen-scratch pass's roster of judged suites, the convention guards'
# exercised roster. Each is declared once in `.freebuff/coverage-readings.mjs`: the id the
# runner keys it by, the sidecar it lands in (`.<id>-coverage.txt`), the env seam a test
# points elsewhere, the prefix its line carries. A dot-file of its own per reading, because
# the readings have separate writers running in parallel workers — written by the guard's
# own close-out, cleared by the runner's test stage at each attempt, read by the runner's
# close and the run page. One rule for all of them, so a reading declared in the registry
# needs no edit here: transient, like the reporter's sidecars above.
.freebuff/.*-coverage.txt
# The poster's record of what it redacted before posting a comment: written beside the body
# it maps to, so CI uploads it with the artifact that holds the raw text. Generated, not kept.
*.redactions.json
# Session scratch and build output, added at the initial commit
.temp/
.vitest-out/
*.tsbuildinfo
.freebuff/*.exe
.freebuff/*.log
.freebuff/*.log.err
